  "notes": "{勝負|しょうぶ} means a match or contest, combining {勝|か}つ (win) and {負|ま}ける (lose).\n\nVERBAL USAGE:\n{勝負|しょうぶ}する means to compete, to have a match.\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {勝負|しょうぶ}しよう: Let's have a match!\n- {勝負|しょうぶ}がつく: the match is decided\n- {勝負|しょうぶ}がつかない: the match isn't decided (a draw)\n- {真剣|しんけん}{勝負|しょうぶ}: serious match\n- {一発|いっぱつ}{勝負|しょうぶ}: one-shot deal, all or nothing\n\nIDIOMS:\n- {勝負|しょうぶ}は{時|とき}の{運|うん}: Victory depends on luck\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {試合|しあい}: match, game (sports)\n- {対決|たいけつ}: confrontation, showdown",
